  "findings": [
    "Grid-frame arithmetic snaps a Float32 midpoint onto the resolution lattice with floor, then grows a frame extent by powers of two, preserving Float32 sum and bound rounding.",
    "Corner reduction preserves source order, ignores absent-distance sentinels and prefers interior contributions over boundary contributions.",
    "The native accumulator initializer copies another mutable global vector. Its value and complete write history are not established by the retained image.",
    "Corner lookup quantizes coordinates into integer keys and uses lexicographic lookup; child creation assigns eight bounds and increments depth. These paths remain untranslated."
  ],
